WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.434
-Here at "The Tonight Show,"
we love songs.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.734
And we especially love songs

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.801
written by our audience members
in under an hour.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:09.000
It's time for "Battle of
the Instant Songwriters."

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.534
Here we go.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:13.334
-♪ Something sung,
and singing the song ♪

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:19.801
♪ And I'm writing the song
about another song ♪

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.801
-Welcome to "Battle of
the Instant Songwriters."

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.234
Before the show,
we went through our audience

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:26.701
and picked out two people
who said they were musicians.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:27.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.701
We gave them each
a made-up song title

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.901
and gave them an hour
to write an original song

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.234
based on that title.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:36.701
Here's a shot of them practicing
backstage a minute ago.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.167
Oh, they're both
playing the piano.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.534
I thought they were
typing out their words.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:41.767
Let's see
what they came up with.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.834
Let's meet them right now.
Come on over, guys.

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.734
Hey, welcome to the show.
Hi.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.033
We doing the elbows?
Is that what we're doing?

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.601
Hi.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.501
-Perfect. Welcome.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.334
Thank you for doing this.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:55.901
I know you didn't know
you were gonna be on the show,

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.501
but here you are, on the show.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:58.667
Let's start with
contestant number one.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.334
What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.567
-I'm Kimberly Denaro.
I'm from Massachusetts.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.901
-Yeah! Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:08.234
Kimberly, welcome to the show.
-Thanks.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.434
-What was the title of the song
that you were given?

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:12.434
-"I'm Scared of my Roomba."

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:13.901
-Ah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.734
That sounds like a hit.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.167
What instrument
will you be playing?

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.868
-The piano.
-All right, very nice.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.834
Why don't you head over there
and get yourself ready to go.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:26.868
And we'll get to hear...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.734
Get ready to go.
What was the name again?

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.801
"I'm Scared of my Roomba"?
Yeah, that's pretty funny.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.000
All right, ladies and gentlemen,
here to perform

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.868
the world premiere
of the soon-to-be classic

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:38.400
"I'm Scared of my Roomba,"
it's Kim Denaro!

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.601
[ Cheer and applause ]

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.100
♪♪

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.367
-♪ In the middle of the night,
I saw it gliding like a ghost ♪

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:52.367
♪ A squeaky shadow
crashing into the corner ♪

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:57.868
♪ Devouring every crumb
in its path ♪

00:01:57.868 --> 00:02:01.601
♪ I told myself
"Oh, don't worry about that ♪

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:03.467
♪ It's probably just a rat ♪

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:08.367
♪ But worse,
it was the Roomba ♪

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:11.434
No!

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:14.901
♪ I'm scared of my Roomba ♪

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.567
♪ I live with a robot ♪

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:19.734
♪ That memorized
the layout of my room ♪

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:24.167
♪ Because I was too
lazy to vacuum ♪

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.334
♪ I took the battery out,
but it's possessed ♪

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:27.901
♪ A hockey puck of suction ♪

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:31.267
♪ Continuing to clean
while plotting my abduction ♪

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:34.834
♪ It's only a matter of time
before the machines take over ♪

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:37.901
♪ And I can't speak the language
of vroom vroom ♪

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:40.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:46.334
♪ But the Roomba of doomba
with it's stomach full of dust ♪

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:52.167
♪ Is a robot that
I'll never trust ♪

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:55.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:57.167
-Kim Denaro.
Come over.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:03:00.434
Kim Denaro!
[ Applause ]

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.467
You wrote a legit song.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:05.167
Very funny.
Thank you, Kim.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.300
All right, let's meet
contestant number two.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.501
What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.701
-My name's Ryder Chasin,
and I'm from Connecticut.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.701
-Yeah, Ryder Chasin
from Connecticut.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.033
Thank you for being here, Ryder.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.033
Ryder, tell everyone
what your song title was.

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:21.968
-Yeah, they gave me "I Bought
an Off-Brand Rapid Test."

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:26.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:27.934
-I feel like I've heard
that song before.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.200
This is amazing.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.968
You will be playing piano,
as well?

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.267
-The electric organ
on the keyboard.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.467
-Oh, I'm so sorry.
Yeah.

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:35.767
-Yeah.
-Thanks for correcting me.

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:36.834
I appreciate it.
-Please, yeah.

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:38.033
-Please, go get ready
to do your --

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.033
-Oh, thank you.
-Go by your electric organ.

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:43.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.567
That's so funny.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:49.300
Ladies and gentlemen, get ready
for the world premiere of

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.567
"I Bought
an Off-Brand Rapid Test,"

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:54.868
done on the electric organ,
by Ryder Chasin.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:58.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:02.601
-♪ Wanted to go Upstate
so I had to validate ♪

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:07.734
♪ That I didn't have the COV ♪

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.367
♪ CVS was out of stock ♪

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.834
♪ So I traveled down the block ♪

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:15.601
♪ And into the Dollar store
I dove ♪

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:16.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.434
♪ I should've known
when they sold it ♪

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.601
♪ Next to staples
and loose screws ♪

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:23.601
♪ I should've known
when the nasal swab said ♪

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:25.300
♪ Warning, slightly used ♪

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.033
♪ I should've known
'cause the brand was something ♪

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.701
♪ I had never seen ♪

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:34.133
♪ And right on the package,
it said COVID-17 ♪

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:35.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.667
♪ Got no clue
if I got the 'rona ♪

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:41.367
♪ Guess I'm staying
home alone...a ♪

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:46.033
♪ 'Cause I bought
an off-brand rapid test ♪

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:49.300
♪ 'Cause I brought an
unplanned, legally banned ♪

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:53.200
♪ Off-brand rapid test ♪

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.801
♪♪

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:59.100
-Wow!

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:02.400
Give it up for Ryder Chasin!

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.801
Thank you very much, Ryder.

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.968
Now it is time to see who won.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:10.033
We're gonna let our great
audience decide the winner.

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.133
Was it Kim Denaro?

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.734
Or was it Ryder Chasin?

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:17.767
[ Loud cheers and applause ]

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.734
It looks like the winner
is Ryder Chasin!

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:20.801
Congratulations, Ryder!

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:22.934
♪♪

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:25.067
Ryder, Congratulations.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:29.300
You will be going home
with $1,000 -- yeah --

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.234
and a "Tonight Show" notebook
for writing more songs.

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:33.300
There you go.
Congratulations.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:38.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.100
-No, no one goes home
empty-handed.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.667
You will also be getting
a notebook with $1,000.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.968
Kim, you write more songs.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.434
And thank you for doing that.
I appreciate it.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:49.200
Give it up for our two
instant songwriters!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.300
Thank you for doing that.
That was amazing!

